# Everything under data/ is reproducible from the commands in README.md.
# The raw archive in particular gets large fast (~170KB per bootstrap fetch,
# and --all writes 656 more files per run).
data/raw/
data/exports/
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
CLAUDE.md
docs/LEARNING.md
# uv.lock IS committed on purpose - it pins exact versions so the project
# rebuilds identically later. Only applications commit lockfiles; libraries
# don't, because they must stay flexible for whoever depends on them.
